WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.721
Cameras and network video recorders provide the visual source.

00:00:04.721 --> 00:00:13.940
Camera resolution, frame rate, field of view, low-light performance, placement, and encoding influence both model accuracy and resource use.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:19.560
An NVR may aggregate streams and retain continuous or event video.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:26.530
RTSP is a common method for delivering live video from cameras and video systems.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:35.299
The AI service connects to an authorized stream, decodes frames, and samples them according to the use case.

00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:39.570
Stream credentials and network paths must be protected.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.292
A local server, workstation, or edge appliance runs inference.

00:00:44.292 --> 00:00:53.060
CPUs can handle lighter workloads, while GPUs or dedicated accelerators improve throughput for larger models and more streams.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:59.131
Capacity planning should include decoding, inference, storage, dashboard use, and peak events.

00:00:59.131 --> 00:01:04.752
Vision models transform frames into detections, classifications, descriptions, or activity observations.

00:01:04.752 --> 00:01:10.372
The surrounding software applies zones, thresholds, schedules, grouping, and business rules.

00:01:10.372 --> 00:01:15.993
Models and rules should be versioned so results can be reproduced.

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:22.513
Storage may hold continuous video, event clips, thumbnails, model metadata, and review outcomes.

00:01:22.513 --> 00:01:29.483
Alerting channels deliver selected events to dashboards, email, mobile applications, or other approved systems.

00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:35.104
Logs record stream health, model errors, user activity, and configuration changes.

00:01:35.104 --> 00:01:45.221
The architecture should show every data flow and trust boundary: camera, network, NVR, inference host, storage, dashboard, alert channel, and administrator.

00:01:45.221 --> 00:01:49.943
Reliable time and camera identity let reviewers correlate events.

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:58.262
Monitoring health is part of the product, because a silent camera or stalled model creates false confidence.
